; Lead: BrokkAi/bifrost-packs#252 (CVE-2022-30631), version-independent part.
; Product source contract: compress/gzip inflates without a size bound, and
; io.ReadAll reads until EOF. A peer that controls a connection therefore
; controls how much memory the program allocates, and a small gzip stream can
; inflate to many gigabytes (CWE-409, CWE-400). Fixed toolchains keep that
; behavior. CVE-2022-30631 (stack exhaustion in gzip Reader.Read) needs
; toolchain evidence the engine does not have (research/osv-dataflow-2026-11/go).
; Scope: the policy reports the connection whether or not it is inflated
; first. A decompression-only policy needs a label added at gzip.NewReader,
; and on Bifrost 0.15.1 a transform on a model-summarized call drops its
; source origin, so the finding cannot be projected (bifrost-dev#9987).
; Engine contract: sources, sinks and the io.LimitReader sanitizer bind
; exactly to the reviewed bifrost.go.stdlib.net, bifrost.go.stdlib.io and
; bifrost.go.stdlib.compress-gzip models. Any other call on the path must be
; modeled, so an unmodeled wrapper such as bufio.NewReader leaves the run
; inconclusive instead of clean. io.Copy is declared but has no summary (the
; schema cannot express its write into dst), so an io.Copy finding is possible
; and its run is inconclusive.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.security.go.network-read-all-unbounded"
  :name "Go network connection read to EOF without a size bound"
  :message "bytes from a network connection, possibly inflated with compress/gzip, are read to EOF without io.LimitReader"
  :severity warning
  :description "Reports net.Dial, net.DialTimeout and net.Listener.Accept connections that reach io.ReadAll or the source of io.Copy, directly or through compress/gzip.NewReader, with no io.LimitReader between them. The peer controls how much is read, and a small gzip stream can inflate without limit (CVE-2022-30631, CWE-409)."
  :tags ["security" "go" "resource-exhaustion" "decompression-bomb" "cwe-400" "cwe-409"]
  :analysis
    (analysis
      :type taint
      :mode may
      :call-modeling (call-modeling :unmodeled require-model)
      :sources
        (endpoint-set
          :entries [
            (source
              :id net-dial
              :display-name "net.Dial connection"
              :categories [io.external]
              :selector
                (rql
                  :schema-version 1
                  (language go
                    (resolved-call
                      :resolves-to "net.Dial"
                      :proof declared
                      (call-bindings
                        (call-shape
                          (call :callee (name "Dial") :arity 2))))))
              :bind (result :index 0)
              :labels [untrusted])
            (source
              :id net-dial-timeout
              :display-name "net.DialTimeout connection"
              :categories [io.external]
              :selector
                (rql
                  :schema-version 1
                  (language go
                    (resolved-call
                      :resolves-to "net.DialTimeout"
                      :proof declared
                      (call-bindings
                        (call-shape
                          (call :callee (name "DialTimeout") :arity 3))))))
              :bind (result :index 0)
              :labels [untrusted])
            (source
              :id net-listener-accept
              :display-name "net.Listener.Accept connection"
              :categories [io.external]
              :selector
                (rql
                  :schema-version 1
                  (language go
                    (resolved-call
                      :resolves-to "net.Listener.Accept"
                      :proof declared
                      (call-bindings
                        (call-shape
                          (call :callee (name "Accept") :arity 0))))))
              :bind (result :index 0)
              :labels [untrusted])])
      :sanitizers
        (endpoint-set
          :entries [
            (sanitizer
              :id io-limit-reader
              :selector
                (rql
                  :schema-version 1
                  (language go
                    (call-argument :formal-index 0
                      (resolved-call
                        :resolves-to "io.LimitReader"
                        :proof declared
                        (call-bindings
                          (call-shape
                            (call :callee (name "LimitReader") :arity 2)))))))
              :input (argument :index 0)
              :output return-value
              :removes [untrusted])])
      :sinks
        (endpoint-set
          :entries [
            (sink
              :id io-read-all-reader
              :display-name "io.ReadAll reader"
              :categories [resource-consumption]
              :selector
                (rql
                  :schema-version 1
                  (language go
                    (call-argument :formal-index 0
                      (resolved-call
                        :resolves-to "io.ReadAll"
                        :proof declared
                        (call-bindings
                          (call-shape
                            (call :callee (name "ReadAll") :arity 1)))))))
              :dangerous-operand (argument :index 0)
              :accepts [untrusted])
            (sink
              :id io-copy-source
              :display-name "io.Copy source reader"
              :categories [resource-consumption]
              :selector
                (rql
                  :schema-version 1
                  (language go
                    (call-argument :formal-index 1
                      (resolved-call
                        :resolves-to "io.Copy"
                        :proof declared
                        (call-bindings
                          (call-shape
                            (call :callee (name "Copy") :arity 2)))))))
              :dangerous-operand (argument :index 1)
              :accepts [untrusted])]))
  :classification
    (classification
      :fallback (classification-id :taxonomy "CWE" :id "400")))
